  2180	/// This is NOT the public [`TransportMessage`] enum — it never adds a variant to
  2181	/// that semver-sensitive type. It only distinguishes an internally-routed
  2182	/// `server/discover` request (which has no public enum variant) from every other
  2183	/// message, so both flow through the SAME POST stages (session → v2 header matrix
  2184	/// → legacy-version → auth → dispatch → event store → response assembly) and
  2185	/// `server/discover` is routed only at the final per-path response-assembly step
  2186	/// (the classify-then-continue design — no pipeline bypass).
  2187	enum HttpIngress {
  2188	    /// Any normal message (typed request, notification, or response) — the
  2189	    /// existing public-enum dispatch path, unchanged.
  2190	    Public(TransportMessage),
  2191	    /// A v2-only `server/discover` request, carrying the ORIGINAL request id.
  2192	    ///
  2193	    /// It does NOT carry a copy of `_meta`: since Phase 113 plan 04 the single
  2194	    /// [`run_v2_header_gate`] reads `params._meta` from the raw body for every
  2195	    /// ingress, so a second captured copy here would be a duplicate read that
  2196	    /// could drift.
  2197	    Discover { id: crate::types::RequestId },
  2198	    /// A `subscriptions/listen` request (Phase 113 plan 10, HTTP-04), carrying
  2199	    /// the ORIGINAL request id — which IS the stream's `subscriptionId` — and the
  2200	    /// RAW `params` value the served branch deserializes into
  2201	    /// [`SubscriptionsListenParams`](crate::types::subscriptions::SubscriptionsListenParams).
  2202	    ///
  2203	    /// Classified here rather than added as a public `ClientRequest` variant:
  2204	    /// Phase 112 established that discipline precisely to keep semver MINOR
  2205	    /// (`enum_variant_added` on a public exhaustive enum is a MAJOR break), and
  2206	    /// `cargo semver-checks` catches a regression. The params stay RAW because
  2207	    /// this classifier must never reject a body — a malformed `params` becomes a
  2208	    /// structured `-32602` in the served branch, after the header gate and auth
  2209	    /// have run, not a parse error before them.
  2210	    SubscriptionsListen {
  2211	        id: crate::types::RequestId,
  2212	        params: Option<serde_json::Value>,
  2213	    },
  2214	    /// A v2-only `tasks/update` request (Phase 114 plan 13, TASK-02), carrying the
  2215	    /// ORIGINAL request id and the RAW `params` the served branch gates over.
  2216	    ///
  2217	    /// Classified through the SHARED
  2218	    /// [`parse_request_or_internal`](crate::shared::protocol_helpers::parse_request_or_internal)
  2219	    /// seam — the `server/discover` route, not this file's `SubscriptionsListen`
  2220	    /// route. `subscriptions/listen` classifies HTTP-locally because it opens an
  2221	    /// HTTP STREAM and has no meaning off this transport; `tasks/update` is an
  2222	    /// ordinary request/response, so its classification belongs in `shared/` where
  2223	    /// a later plan can widen its transport reach without a semver break.
  2224	    ///
  2225	    /// Not a public `ClientRequest` variant for the reason Phase 112 recorded on
  2226	    /// [`Discover`](Self::Discover)'s sibling: `enum_variant_added` on a public
  2227	    /// exhaustive enum is a MAJOR break, and `cargo semver-checks` catches a
  2228	    /// regression. The params stay RAW because the classifier must never reject a
  2229	    /// body — a malformed `params` becomes a structured `-32602` in the served
  2230	    /// branch, AFTER the era, backend, declaration and auth gates have run, not a
  2231	    /// parse error before them.
  2232	    TasksUpdate {
  2233	        id: crate::types::RequestId,
  2234	        params: serde_json::Value,
  2235	    },
  2236	}
